<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahasi Sayadaw</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1904">1904</a>–<a href="/years/1982">1982</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mahasi Sayadaw was a Burmese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theravada-buddhism">Theravada</a> Buddhist monk and meditation master. His method of insight, or vipassana, meditation, based on noting bodily and mental events, was taught at a centre in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Rangoon</a> from 1949 and spread across Asia and the West. He also played a leading part in the Sixth Buddhist Council held in Rangoon in 1954–1956.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahasi-sayadaw.jpg" alt="Mahasi Sayadaw" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahasi_Sayadaw.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Burmese Buddhist scholarship and meditation teachers, notably <b>Mahasi Sayadaw</b> and the lay teacher S.N. Goenka, who trained in Burma, spread vipassana meditation worldwide.</blockquote><a href="/empire/myanmar">Myanmar · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Shwebo District, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangon">Yangon</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=23.2,95.52&amp;year=1954" aria-label="Shwebo District on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7100 1308 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Mahasi Sayadaw"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7550 1578h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7550 1578h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=23.2,95.52&amp;year=1954">What was here in 1954? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
